{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390770-a-dead-world-of-soul-steel","id":1390770,"title":"A dead world of Soul Steel","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-22T07:56:00-07:00","id":1390770,"title":"A dead world of Soul Steel","content":"This post is inspired by this <a href=\"https://getpocket.com/explore/item/four-reasons-you-shouldn-t-exist?utm_source=pocket-newtab\" target=\"_blank\">click-bait article</a> I'm reading about how little differences in our universe would make it impossible for us to exist. It got me to remembering the old write-up of the World of Darkness' Neverborn as the ghosts of stillborn universes.<br /> <br /> What if an Exalt, traveling deep into the Wyld, discovered a failed, early attempt by the Primordials to make Creation? A world that is made of Soul Steel or even stranger, more alien &amp; ruined geography?<br /> <br /> What if this world possesses a ghost? An ancient &amp; terrible spirit, truly never-born.<br /> <br /> What fun horrors could be concocted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4428,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","user":"Daredevil","date":". 05-22-2020, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T12:04:14-07:00","id":1390824,"title":"","content":"You know about Zen-Mu, right? What you're describing sounds a lot like it and I'm not sure if you already know about their first world and consider this a different failed attempt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T13:08:00-07:00","id":1390835,"title":"","content":"I don't think that was really a failed attempt at making Creation, was it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-22T13:31:32-07:00","id":1390841,"title":"","content":"It's an earlier attempt at creating a world that the Primordials considered a failure, hence why I'm trying to determine if Daredevil knows about it. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T01:33:09-07:00","id":1390932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390770-a-dead-world-of-soul-steel?p=1390824#post1390824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know about Zen-Mu, right? What you're describing sounds a lot like it and I'm not sure if you already know about their first world and consider this a different failed attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a vague recollection of a previous attempt. Thank you for reminding me of the particulars. It is strange when I am confronted with the rich lore of this setting I have curiously forgotten.<br /> <br /> This would be another attempt, more bleak. Are perhaps something tried before Zen-Mu, an early non-start they don't even consider a full attempt. But perhaps that failure does not see itself as something below consideration as even an experiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T05:06:19-07:00","id":1390954,"title":"","content":"We played a cross-over game (well, 3, each about 4-5 sessions) set in 3 pre-Creation worlds the Primordials had made as practice and then discarded, but they were weird and freaky rather than bleak and dead, so I'm not sure it's what you want.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T05:50:22-07:00","id":1390956,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390770-a-dead-world-of-soul-steel?p=1390954#post1390954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure it's what you want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spit balling &amp; conversation.<br /> <br /> What kind of strange effects could this blighted world have on PC's?<br /> <br /> Is there anything of value to temp investigation &amp; plunder?<br /> <br /> The game you played sounds very cool &amp; ambitious. Could you share some details? I'd love to hear how the ST sold the freakish &amp; weird elements.<br /> <br /> Did he reveal why the Primordials discarded each one?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4428-daredevil","name":"Daredevil","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4428_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"404"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-23T05:59:30-07:00","id":1390962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390770-a-dead-world-of-soul-steel#post1390770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This post is inspired by this <a href=\"https://getpocket.com/explore/item/four-reasons-you-shouldn-t-exist?utm_source=pocket-newtab\" target=\"_blank\">click-bait article</a> I'm reading about how little differences in our universe would make it impossible for us to exist. It got me to remembering the old write-up of the World of Darkness' Neverborn as the ghosts of stillborn universes.<br /> <br /> What if an Exalt, traveling deep into the Wyld, discovered a failed, early attempt by the Primordials to make Creation? A world that is made of Soul Steel or even stranger, more alien &amp; ruined geography?<br /> <br /> What if this world possesses a ghost? An ancient &amp; terrible spirit, truly never-born.<br /> <br /> What fun horrors could be concocted?</div> </div> </div> </div>A Stillborn Creation is a very evocative concept. Maybe a mix of Soulsteel and Gossamer!?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-24T15:25:05-07:00","id":1391287,"title":"","content":"deep in the wyld there are horrors and wonders that amaze even the Raksha. Even during the first age, when reality shaping engines pushed back the chaos, the merest speck of the collected wonders were found. And when the exalted sought knowledge, there was no boundery they would not cross. So did a small conclave of Solars and Lunars sought the origin of Soulsteel. They were not content with the explinations of the underworld and the forgotten race. They wanted to know how Autocthon even knew of soulsteel, as it clearly was an established process. They interrogated many Raksha to find this out. And one told them of a horrorible place that all avoided. A lifeless place made of screaming metal. Amongst the worlds the Primordials made before Zen-Mu lurks a sphere made entirely of soulsteel. No Primordial claims responsibility for this place, and it is only called the Dead World. Nothing exists here save Soulsteel, and whoever created it abandoned it soon after. Occasionally a Deathlord will send a Abyssal deep into the Wyld in search of this el dorado, none beliefing it anything more than a Faerie tale. But it is real, and something malevolent looks jealously at the life filled Creation from within this unholy abomination.<br /> <br /> ------ <br /> <br /> this just something I threw together. maybe I will make more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-25T02:21:06-07:00","id":1391447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daredevil</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390770-a-dead-world-of-soul-steel?p=1390956#post1390956\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game you played sounds very cool &amp; ambitious. Could you share some details? I'd love to hear how the ST sold the freakish &amp; weird elements.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so this was a crossover game between 3 different Exalted games, 2 STs.<br /> <br /> So we had 3 games, each ran for about a story, each with 6-7 characters drawn from a mix of the 3 games.<br /> <br /> My Zenith Alazar and his companion Cid found themselves on a floating island over a great void, where they met a Lunar and two Solars from an alternative Creation, and a Solar from a third world. There were hundreds of floating islands, which slowly drifted up from the frozen void towards a red sun covered in screaming faces with huge hungry mouths. As the islands rose, they defrosted, awakening a variety of talking animals from slumber. These animals sometimes got on, sometimes ate each other. However, as the islands got closer to the sun they'd try to jump down to other islands, because eventually the islands would fall up in the mouths of the sun and burn up.<br /> The sun was inhabited by an ancient smith who sent clockwork angels out to do his will, while much lower down the Queen of Air and Darkness ruled a realm of predators by her pacts with the spirits of the dark void.<br /> <br /> My Twilight Shadow of Kings however, escaped his own world (because he was being chased by his clone who wanted to eat him because there can only be one, long story) deliberately, and became chief advisor to the Tree-King. This was on a large island surrounded by an eternal sea. Instead of a sun and stars, it had a huge pillar of light in the centre of the island which rotated. The five peoples of the island (huge blue giants, fish-people who need land to spawn, ent-like tree people, halfling-sized golem-suits of armour, and eusocial lizards) lived in peace under the yellow light. But then a Dawn from another world arrived and incited the fish-people to war. At about the same time, the light of the sun-pillar turned red. The seas began to rise, pushing the five peoples to war over territory to flee the rising waters. Shadow of Kings began producing magitek chips to put inside the peaceful tree-people to help them fight. Then he met some Solars and a Dragonblood from alternative Creations and after some conflict we worked to take down the Dawn and create a new island via sorcery, and arks to take the people there. I learnt that over time the pillar changes between the colours of the Five Maidens, each creating a period associated with that Maiden (a time of trade and migration, a time of war, etc).<br /> <br /> The other ST took a slightly different approach.<br /> <br /> My Full Moon Dr Soma woke up in a jungle surrounded by Solars from other worlds. They explored and discovered that, again, this was a realm of talking animals who'd overthrown and destroyed humanity at the command of the Sea People. While there were some ancient and mysterious ruins which we explored a bit later, we spent most of our time trying to expel the Pigs, Dogs, Cats and Swans of the Animalist State who'd come across the sea to conquer the local Monkeys and Snakes, or as they saw it, enlighten them by killing the humans and establishing True Animalism, where all animals are equal (but maybe pigs are more equal than others...). Their battle groups with rifles and machine guns were slightly tricky, but our combat-Exalts didn't have too much difficulty, so we soon expelled them from the city and then fought them through the jungle.<br /> But Professor Python and his rebels (who had some kind of vague ideological link to the Meowist State across the mountains) then unleashed a further revolution, with monkey suicide bombers and assassins, and all got quite messy.<br /> In the end, however, a tenuous peace deal was worked out between the various political factions, and Luna took us back to our own world.<br /> <br /> After we'd all escaped, we met up in a world beyond the worlds, where we met some other Solars and Lunars, who'd also been in strange worlds. The only one I remember was a giant city where golems fought over a massive library of stone tablets where the secrets of many worlds were written. There were others I think, just can't remember them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did he reveal why the Primordials discarded each one?<br /> </div> </div> </div>No. It was 3-5 sessions for each, and the main plot was how to escape, or rather how to pass the Incarnae's tests of righteousness to earn an escape.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-11T10:50:25-07:00","id":1417658,"title":"","content":"First thing that crosses my mind is that soulsteel requires actually dying, what calls for being alive/born first, imho. Also thinking that Cajerron, the world created by rogue Primordial Cemunian, Constellation of Sinew and Dream, as a big &quot;F**k you all&quot; gesture to its Primordial kin and obliterated by the UCS in the Time of the Titans might fit with the imagery even better than Zen-Mu.<br /> <br /> In my own 2e Sidereal game i did conceive a weird cosmic threat that was kind of like you describe too, just found a summary.<br /> <br /> <i><b>Ozymandias</b>, <b>the Omphalos that Lives</b>, a world long abandoned by its primordial makers, where the concentrated mass and pressure of countless millions of never used jade eggs would result in their fusion with that world's core, sparking the awakening of its self, as a being capable of life, awareness, thought and deed, a world born already close to extinction, lonely and desirous for gods, mortals, plants and beasts to inhabit, build, destroy, love, hate, live and die in its expanses and feed its hunger for the flowing essence and companionship to fill its places of power and solitary existence.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 10-12-2020, 10:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T09:57:29-07:00","id":1418385,"title":"","content":"Well, they can always be really fascinating artifact components for whatever you want to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T13:12:09-07:00","id":1418406,"title":"","content":"I read the title and immediately thought of Mirrodin from Magic: The Gathering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1520732-forged-by-purpose-alchemicals-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Forged By Purpose: The Alchemicals</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1413451-dead-but-not-gone-ghosts\" target=\"_blank\">Dead But Not Gone: Ghosts</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/228291-ghosts-a-revision-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Ghosts: A Revision</a> (2nd Edition)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/316-masters-of-the-industrial-elements-2e-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Masters of the Industrial Elements</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1157362-from-the-crucible-crafting-as-a-struggle-peach\" target=\"_blank\">\u200bFrom The Crucible: Crafting As A Struggle</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/74-kyeudo","name":"Kyeudo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar74_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1723"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T05:32:06-07:00","id":1418503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyeudo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1390770-a-dead-world-of-soul-steel?p=1418406#post1418406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I read the title and immediately thought of Mirrodin from Magic: The Gathering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great minds etc., I read this thread months ago and didn't have anything interesting to contribute, saw it pop back to the top today and said &quot;oh right, Mirrodin&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://media.wizards.com/images/magic/som/factionwars/hotspots/lg/131573b.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://media.wizards.com/images/mag...lg/131573b.jpg</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://media.wizards.com/images/magic/som/factionwars/hotspots/lg/131581b.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">https://media.wizards.com/images/mag...lg/131581b.jpg</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://magic.wizards.com/en/articles/archive/savor-flavor/world-sculpted-metal-2011-03-23\" target=\"_blank\">https://magic.wizards.com/en/article...tal-2011-03-23</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":456,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","user":"Blackwell","date":". 10-16-2020, 09:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}